{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550282-how-do-you-feel-about-storytellers-also-playing-characters","id":1550282,"title":"How do you feel about Storytellers also playing characters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-20T01:06:00-07:00","id":1550282,"title":"How do you feel about Storytellers also playing characters?","content":"I have two recruits for an HtR (1e) chronicle, and I'm wondering if this is enough to start the chronicle. However, since they are both fairly new to RP'ing, I thought I would also create a few characters that can work alongside them to help them stay &quot;on the rails&quot; and sort of guide them within the game, without specifically being only an outside voice for rules (as I feel like this would break immersion too much).<br /> <br /> So my question is: is it acceptable for an ST to also play a character in the same chronicle they are running? Would this be the same as having NPCs that the characters will interact with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26060-nuhxnger36","name":"NuHxnger36","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T09:37:38-07:00","id":1550286,"title":"","content":"So, it sounds like you're asking about GMPCs as most TTRPG people would call them.<br /> <br /> Are they acceptable? Exceptionally up for debate. Some people consider GMPCs inherently crossing the line from good NPCs to poorly used NPCs. Most people are somewhere in the middle. Some games have them as a default part of the design.<br /> <br /> A lot of definitions of what a GMPC is vs. a normal NPC betrays the biases of the authors regarding them.<br /> <br /> That all said, I don't think they're really that necessary for HtR. HtR is pretty flexible. While PCs are usually going to put all of their primary Virtue points into their Creed's Edges to get the higher level powers of their archetype, that leaves them with two tracks of Virtues to spend on useful Edges that don't all have to be gunning for a narrow set. The Imbued are also purposefully designed to be hit or miss on having the right power for the job at hand. Even with five PCs you're supposed to have situations where nobody can solve the problem with a smart application of an Edge and it comes down to some Second Sight and a bunch of smarts and luck. As the ST, you also have a lot of control over how potent the enemies your players are going to face are. HtR has one of the more robust WoD enemy building rules, so you can more easily tailor your antagonists to your players' interests. <br /> <br /> HtR also comes with plenty of Backgrounds to serve as sources of exposition and help so the players avoid too many big mistakes (esp. if you include the Creedbook ones).<br /> <br /> My suggestion? Talk to your two players. Their fun matters more than the forumites' opinions on GMPCs. If they like the idea and you can set some solid ground rules for yourself to make sure you don't overshadow them, see how it goes. If they're not grooving on it, you have lots of other tools thanks to the game you picked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-21T16:35:08-07:00","id":1550305,"title":"","content":"Depends on the ST's intentions; for my NPCs, I make out full blown characters and integrate them into the story; the PCs are always the stars and the NPCs, supporting characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T00:32:37-07:00","id":1550428,"title":"","content":"Depends really on the type of game you are running and the type of character.<br /> <br /> If you mostly doing social interaction it doesn't really work imo.<br /> <br /> If you are mostly &quot;Dungeon Crawling&quot; and have a small party it can work.<br /> <br /> In general the character shouldn't be the &quot;Face&quot;, and should not the be the only combat focused character in the party (and not overshadow the others).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}